{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1360118-what-equipment-do-you-start-with","id":1360118,"title":"What equipment do you start with?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-10T06:40:04-08:00","id":1360118,"title":"What equipment do you start with?","content":"In either \u00c6on or the core how do you determine reasonable starting equipment? I noticed that lacking wealth or other \u201cyou get gear\u201d doesn\u2019t seem to limit you that much when I was reading the ready made characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T09:32:22-08:00","id":1360141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werlynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1360118-what-equipment-do-you-start-with#post1360118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In either \u00c6on or the core how do you determine reasonable starting equipment? I noticed that lacking wealth or other \u201cyou get gear\u201d doesn\u2019t seem to limit you that much when I was reading the ready made characters.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's part of the &quot;Access&quot; portion of your paths. You are reasonably equipped for your job. It is mentioned in the Path portion of Character Creation, and on page 40.<br /> <br /> Alternatively you can handle it through personal Wealth, or the Patron Edge. Artifact is also good if you want some super science gear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T19:35:40-08:00","id":1360272,"title":"","content":"I looked at the access thing as a thing you do during game. I\u2019ll reread","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T20:59:52-08:00","id":1360283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werlynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1360118-what-equipment-do-you-start-with?p=1360272#post1360272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I looked at the access thing as a thing you do during game. I\u2019ll reread</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll admit, It could be better spelled out, and I think a way it is phrased over in Scion makes it more explicit.<br /> <br /> You can also look to the example characters in the Ready Made Character supplement that just released, and see that they have modest equipment selections regardless of Wealth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-11T07:38:03-08:00","id":1360316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1360118-what-equipment-do-you-start-with?p=1360283#post1360283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll admit, It could be better spelled out, and I think a way it is phrased over in Scion makes it more explicit.<br /> <br /> You can also look to the example characters in the Ready Made Character supplement that just released, and see that they have modest equipment selections regardless of Wealth.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a &quot;rule of thumb&quot; I figure you can treat initial Path levels + 1 as &quot;Wealth&quot; for the purpose of initial stuff on a case by case basis. So, any 1 Dot or 2 Dot items that would make sense for the Path are okay - but they need to be bog-standard, easily available things. A Sneak might get lockpicks, etc. Specialized stuff requires Wealth, Patron, Artifact, etc.<br /> <br /> One thing I'll allow my players to do is trade in their Step 6 Attribute + 3 Edges for an extra Path dot, giving them one non-Path edge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","user":"johntfs","date":". 01-11-2020, 10:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-11T09:11:59-08:00","id":1360328,"title":"","content":"An extra path dot grants a bunch of skill and edge points doesn\u2019t it? That seems like a pretty easy trade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-11T17:34:51-08:00","id":1360407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werlynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1360118-what-equipment-do-you-start-with?p=1360328#post1360328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An extra path dot grants a bunch of skill and edge points doesn\u2019t it? That seems like a pretty easy trade.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. An addition Path dot costs 18 XP. Buying 3 Skill Dots and two Path Edge Dots costs 19 XP. Making the trade costs an Attribute Dot and three non-Path Edge Dots, which total up to be 19 XP. So, waiting to improve the Path score in-game saves 1 XP. Which isn't much, granted.<br /> <br /> It really depends on your priorities. Extra skill points can be very useful given that Attribute+Skill is your dice pool and Enhancements are irrelevant unless you generate at least one success. Plus you're still getting two Dots in Path Edges for whatever Path it is. Beyond all that, it boosts your Contacts in that Path, making it more likely that said Contact will be useful to you in-game.<br /> <br /> One the other hand, if you're playing a Psion and especially a Teleporter or Quatakinetic, you'll want/need to use that Attribute point at Step 6 to boost your Psi to a 3. That leaves you four non-Path Edge Dots. That's a 4 Dot Super-science Artifact if you want it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-11T19:49:07-08:00","id":1360432,"title":"","content":"I would use the paths as guidelines for equipments, not just what they carry around but also what they have at home and access at their jobs. It\u2019s a rule of thumb, but it\u2019s simple, the more paths you have that would offer the equipment, more you can spend on it. The idea is kind of, add the relevant path dots and wealth, the wealth edge and twice the patron, if it costs equal or less, you can have it.<br /> <br /> A police officer (society path) for sure have a gun all the time, if he has a military family (military brat path) the gun is probably bigger than one a regular police officer would have, and if he is a combat specialist (role path) even bigger. Not spending any wealth.<br /> <br /> For some equipments specially restricted, like a tank or a fighter jet, you probably need a favor from a powerful contact for temporary use, or a Patron with proper contacts, or a wealth high enough and a proper contact. But that would be a kind of extreme situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}